{% aside type="caution" title="In development" %}
This architecture is still changing. Check the
[milu](https://github.com/hhandika/milu) and
[NAHPU API](https://github.com/nahpu/nahpu_api) repositories for the latest
code.
{% /aside %}

Model training is split between a thin command line front end and a shared
library. milu handles commands, configuration files, and reports.
Models, data loading, and weight storage live in the `nahpu_dl` crate of the
NAHPU API, so the NAHPU app can run the same models that milu trains.

```text
milu (command line)           nahpu_dl (NAHPU API)             Model package
├── cli/   arguments    ──▶   ├── models/   networks     ──▶   ├── manifest.toml
└── core/  workflow steps     ├── data/     loaders            └── model.bpk
    ├── train                 ├── finetune  training               (or model.safetensors)
    ├── test                  ├── evaluate  metrics
    ├── infer                 ├── predict   inference
    ├── embed                 ├── embed     embeddings
    ├── models                ├── store     weights
    └── convert               ├── manifest  package metadata
                              └── hub       pretrained downloads
```

Each milu workflow step in `core/<step>/` has a runner (`mod.rs`), a config
writer (`init.rs`), config types and defaults (`configs.rs`), summaries
(`reports.rs`), and one file per backend. Any change to how a model is built,
trained, or stored belongs in `nahpu_dl`, not in milu.

## Model packages

Every trained model is a directory with a manifest and one weight file:

```text
skull_genus/
├── manifest.toml
└── model.bpk        # or model.safetensors
```

The manifest records everything needed to load the model without extra
configuration:

| Field              | Description                                               |
| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| `name`             | Human-readable model name                                 |
| `nahpu_dl_version` | Version of `nahpu_dl` that wrote the package               |
| `modality`         | Kind of input the model takes (table or image)            |
| `task`             | What the model predicts                                   |
| `architecture`     | Network architecture and its hyperparameters              |
| `labels`           | Class labels in output order; empty for regression        |
| `preprocessing`    | How raw inputs are turned into tensors                    |
| `weights`          | The package's weight file                                 |
| `embedding_dim`    | Size of the embedding vector produced by the backbone     |
| `metrics`          | Summary metrics from the last evaluation                  |
| `provenance`       | Where the model came from                                 |

## Models

- **Tabular:** multilayer perceptron.
- **Images:** ResNet-18, 34, 50, 101, and 152, and MobileNetV2.
  ImageNet-pretrained weights can be imported from torchvision or timm
  checkpoints, or downloaded from the Hugging Face Hub.

## Data sources

- CSV or TSV tables with a header row, such as specimen measurements.
- Image folders with one sub-directory of images per class.
- Extracted NAHPU data packages, where specimen photos are labeled by the
  specimen's taxon at a chosen rank.

## Backends and features

`nahpu_dl` is built on [Burn](https://burn.dev). Cargo features select the
backend and optional parts:

| Feature          | Purpose                                                     |
| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| `flex` (default) | Pure-Rust CPU backend, multithreaded                        |
| `wgpu`           | GPU backend through Vulkan, Metal, or DX12                  |
| `cuda`           | CUDA backend                                                |
| `train`          | Fine-tuning; off by default so inference-only builds stay small |
| `hub`            | Download pretrained models from the Hugging Face Hub        |

## Workflow

| Command                                | What it does                                          |
| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| `milu train init`                      | Writes a training config (`milu_train.toml`)          |
| `milu train run`                       | Trains or fine-tunes and writes a model package       |
| `milu test`                            | Evaluates a model and writes JSON and CSV reports     |
| `milu infer`                           | Writes predictions as CSV or JSON, with top-k labels  |
| `milu embed`                           | Writes embeddings as CSV or JSON lines                |
| `milu models list` / `pull` / `import` | Finds, downloads, or converts pretrained models       |
| `milu models info`                     | Shows what a model package contains                   |
| `milu convert`                         | Rewrites weights as burnpack or SafeTensors           |

Model packages are written to `out_models/`, and test, inference, and
embedding results to `milu_results/`. See
[Fine-tuning](/en/contributing/model-training/fine-tuning/) for training
options.
